>> title: Pork Liver Pâté
>> category: Dressings & Dips
>> tags: pork, liver, vietnamese, terrine, oven
>> servings: 12
>> time: 16 hr
>> slack: unforgiving — a terrine is baked to 160°F at the centre and held cold afterwards, and getting that wrong is a safety failure rather than a texture one
>> counters: Phở & Bánh Mì, Deli
>> aka: pâté, liver pâté, pate, the spread in a bánh mì, pa tê, banh mi pate, pork liver pate, bò pâté, country pâté
>> pairs-with: baguette, do-chua

>> step: preheat oven 325°F (165°C)
Preheat the #oven{} to 325°F (165°C).

>> step: soak cold 2 hr, drain
Soak @pork liver{1%lb}(450 g; trimmed of ducts and cut in chunks) in @whole milk{2%cup}(475 mL) in the #fridge{} for ~soak{2%hr}, then drain and pat dry.

>> step: sweat 10 min, no colour
Sweat @shallots{4%large}(about 1 cup, sliced) and @garlic{6%cloves}(sliced) in @unsalted butter{2%Tbs}(30 g) in a #skillet{} over low heat for ~sweat{10%min}, until soft and sweet with no colour on them.

>> step: grind coarse
Grind @&(~2)drained liver{}, @&(~1)aromatics{}, @fatty pork shoulder{8%oz}(225 g; cut in 1-inch cubes) and @diced pork fatback{8%oz}(225 g) in a #food processor{} to a coarse paste still flecked with fat — this is a country pâté, not a mousse.

>> step: pulse in
Pulse @eggs{2%large}, @heavy cream{1/3%cup}(80 mL), @fish sauce{2%Tbs}(30 mL), @brandy{2%Tbs}(30 mL), @five-spice powder{1%tsp}, @kosher salt{1%Tbs}(10 g), @black pepper{1%tsp}(coarsely ground) and @sugar{1%tsp} into @&(~1)paste{} in short bursts.

>> step: line the terrine, bake 90 min in a water bath
Line a #terrine{} with @sliced pork fatback{6%oz}(170 g; cut thin, or streaky bacon), pack @&(~1)forcemeat{} in and fold the ends over, then stand the covered terrine in a #roasting pan{} of boiling water and ~bake{90%min} to 160°F (71°C).

>> step: weight, chill 12 hr
Weight @&(~1)baked pâté{} with a foil-wrapped brick and chill ~chill{12%hr}, overnight, before turning it out.
